WEBVTT

00:09.000 --> 00:12.160
Plug the receiver into the USB-C port on your phone

00:12.720 --> 00:15.919
The TX status LED on the receiver will turn on

00:16.120 --> 00:18.320
and your phone will then power the receiver

00:20.839 --> 00:24.359
The receiver can link with up to two transmitters (same or different models)

00:24.640 --> 00:26.760
When the LED on the receiver is green

00:27.039 --> 00:30.640
the receiver can link with two DJI Mic Mini transmitters

00:31.399 --> 00:32.840
When the LED is blue

00:32.840 --> 00:34.359
the receiver can link with:

00:34.600 --> 00:36.719
Two DJI Mic 3 transmitters

00:37.560 --> 00:42.119
OR One DJI Mic Mini and one DJI Mic 3 transmitter

00:47.880 --> 00:50.759
Double-press the linking button to change the LED color

00:52.799 --> 00:53.759
As an example

00:53.880 --> 00:57.840
here are the steps to link the receiver with one DJI Mic Mini transmitter

00:57.840 --> 01:00.200
and one DJI Mic 3 transmitter

01:01.079 --> 01:03.320
Check the LED color on the receiver

01:03.479 --> 01:05.760
If the LED blinks green slowly

01:05.799 --> 01:08.359
double-press the linking button to switch to blue

01:10.280 --> 01:12.560
Then hold the linking button to start linking

01:20.200 --> 01:21.560
When transmitter is on

01:21.760 --> 01:24.959
press and hold the linking button on the transmitter for two seconds

01:24.959 --> 01:29.079
until the system status LED blinks blue and green alternately

01:30.480 --> 01:31.959
Once successfully linked

01:31.959 --> 01:33.840
the LEDs will turn solid

01:37.200 --> 01:41.359
Attach the transmitter to clothing using the clip or magnet

01:43.079 --> 01:45.760
The transmitter can then capture audio for the phone

01:46.959 --> 01:49.840
The receiver has a noise cancellation mode switch

01:50.519 --> 01:52.799
Toggle to switch between different modes:

01:54.400 --> 01:57.400
O (Off) means noise cancellation is disabled

01:57.480 --> 02:00.120
L (Low) provides weak noise cancellation

02:00.359 --> 02:02.959
H (High) gives strong noise cancellation

02:03.760 --> 02:07.680
Open the DJI Mimo App (v2.5.0 or later) to access Wireless Microphone interface

02:07.680 --> 02:10.120
and adjust settings such as channel and gain

02:11.080 --> 02:12.159
During recording

02:12.159 --> 02:16.159
you can connect an analog USB-C headset to the receiver charging port

02:16.159 --> 02:17.919
for real-time audio monitoring

02:18.400 --> 02:20.759
For extended filming or livestreaming

02:20.840 --> 02:23.599
it is recommended to charge your phone via this port

02:27.039 --> 02:31.159
Open the DJI Mimo app and go to the Wireless Microphone interface

02:31.520 --> 02:34.719
Tap the icon in the top-right corner to view the device name

02:35.039 --> 02:37.919
serial numbers and firmware versions

02:38.280 --> 02:41.919
Tap the firmware version to download and install the latest version
